# Stacks 070S (1) for an arbitrary sheaf of modules

Let `S` be a scheme and `F` an arbitrary sheaf of `𝒪_S`-modules.  Stacks Lemma 070S (1) says
that for each `τ ∈ {Zariski, étale, smooth, syntomic, fppf}` the pullback of `F` along the
morphism of ringed sites `id_{τ,Zar} : ((Sch/S)_τ, 𝒪) → (S_Zar, 𝒪_S)` is the
`τ`-sheafification of the presheaf `(f : T → S) ↦ Γ(T, f^*F)`.  The pullback is the
`τ`-sheafification of the pullback of presheaves of modules, so the lemma is the assertion that
a single comparison morphism of presheaves of modules — the transpose, under
`CategoryTheory.PresheafOfModules.pullbackPushforwardAdjunction`, of the map pulling a section of
`F` over an open `U` of `S` back to the open subscheme `U` — is locally bijective for every `τ`.

Both halves hold with no hypothesis on `F`.

* *Local surjectivity.*  A section of `f^*F` is, locally on the source, a combination of
  pullbacks of sections of `F` over one open of the base
  (`AlgebraicGeometry.exists_span_pullbackSection`, which uses the local surjectivity of the
  Zariski sheafification of the presheaf-level pullback and the fact that the presheaf-level
  pullback is generated by the image of the unit).  Over the opens where that happens the section
  is in the image of the comparison.
* *Local injectivity.*  Every section of the presheaf-level pullback lies in the span of the
  generators indexed by one open `W` of `S`.  Over `W` the generators are the images, under a
  transpose `β` of the unit along the inclusion of the small Zariski site of the object, of
  sections of the presheaf-level pullback on that small site; two sections with the same image
  under the comparison come from two such sections with the same image in the Zariski
  sheafification, which therefore agree on a Zariski covering, and `β` carries the agreement
  back to a covering of the big site.

The opens involved are open immersions, so they form a covering for each of the five
topologies, and every statement is made at a general `τ`.

## Main definitions

* `AlgebraicGeometry.openSubSections`: a section of `f^*F` over an open `V` of `Y`, read as a
  section of `(V.ι ≫ f)^*F` over all of the open subscheme `V`.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.BigFppfOver.pullbackSectionsUnit`: pulling sections back, as a morphism
  from `F` to the restriction of `AlgebraicGeometry.BigFppfOver.pullbackSectionsPresheaf` to
  the small Zariski site.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.BigFppfOver.pullbackSectionsComparison`: **the comparison of Stacks 070S
  (1)**, the transpose of `pullbackSectionsUnit` across the pullback--pushforward adjunction.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.BigFppfOver.sectionSubordinateCover`: the Zariski covering of an object by
  the opens over which a given section is a combination of pullbacks of sections of `F` over
  one open of `S`.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.BigFppfOver.presheafPullback`,
  `AlgebraicGeometry.BigFppfOver.presheafPullbackUnit` and
  `AlgebraicGeometry.BigFppfOver.presheafPullbackGenerator`: the source of the comparison, the
  unit of the adjunction at `F`, and the generators of the source.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.BigFppfOver.openSubFunctor`,
  `AlgebraicGeometry.BigFppfOver.openSubStructureMap` and
  `AlgebraicGeometry.BigFppfOver.openSubBeta`: the opens of an object as a functor into the big
  site, the ring comparison along it, and the transpose `β` of the generators.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.BigFppfOver.zariskiEqualizerCover`: the covering on which two sections with
  the same image under the comparison agree.

## Main results

* `AlgebraicGeometry.exists_span_pullbackSection`: sections of a pullback are locally
  combinations of pulled-back sections, for an arbitrary module.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.BigFppfOver.isLocallySurjective_pullbackSectionsComparison` and
  `AlgebraicGeometry.BigFppfOver.isLocallyInjective_pullbackSectionsComparison`: the comparison
  is locally bijective for every `τ`.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.BigFppfOver.isIso_baseSheafification_map_pullbackSectionsComparison`: its
  `τ`-sheafification is an isomorphism.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.BigFppfOver.baseAssociatedModuleIsoPullbackSections`: **Stacks 070S (1)**
  for an arbitrary sheaf of `𝒪_S`-modules and every `τ`.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.BigFppfOver.sectionsComparison_eq_pullbackSectionsComparison`: for a
  quasi-coherent `F` the comparison is `AlgebraicGeometry.BigFppfOver.sectionsComparison`.

## Implementation notes

The quasi-coherent form of the lemma,
`AlgebraicGeometry.BigFppfOver.baseAssociatedModuleIsoSections`, is proved through the affine
base-change description of the sections of a pullback, which needs quasi-coherence.  The
argument here replaces it by the local generation statement above and by the transpose `β`,
neither of which sees any hypothesis on `F`; its target
`AlgebraicGeometry.BigFppfOver.pullbackSectionsPresheaf` agrees with
`AlgebraicGeometry.BigFppfOver.sectionsPresheafOfModules` by definition when `F` is
quasi-coherent.

